WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:08.040
I am very excited about this paper. So what does&nbsp;
it do? Magic, according to the authors! That is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:14.400
not text to image, where we write a text&nbsp;
prompt and get a beautiful photo or painting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:23.520
but something else: text to 3D. Hmm…now that&nbsp;
would be fantastic, I would say it qualifies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:31.320
as magic. We write something and out comes 3D&nbsp;
geometry that we can put into a video game or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:38.160
any kind of virtual world. Teleconferencing.&nbsp;
Anything you wish. Dear Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.920
this is Two Minute Papers with Dr. Károly&nbsp;
Zsolnai-Fehér. Now, wait a second. The previous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.640
DreamFusion technique was capable of&nbsp;
doing that. And this was a paper that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:56.720
was published just a year ago. Now, yes, but&nbsp;
this one has two problems. Problem number one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:03.480
it takes a long time, and problem&nbsp;
number two, we still get coarse results.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:10.880
Now, does this paper really have the magic they&nbsp;
promised? Let’s have a look together! Whoa!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.720
Look at that difference. I immediately&nbsp;
see that this has so much more detail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:24.640
it has 8 times higher resolution than the previous&nbsp;
method. And it gets better, we noted earlier that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:33.080
they are not only coarse, but slow too. The&nbsp;
coarseness is gone, fantastic, but I imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:40.200
that this is now probably even slower in return.&nbsp;
We don’t get all this quality for free, do we?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:50.360
That cannot be true. Whoa! It is not only free, it&nbsp;
is even twice as fast as the previous technique.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:57.720
I also love the variety of objects it can conjure&nbsp;
up. We can even ask for more imaginative things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:05.160
like a car made out of sushi. That’s good. Now,&nbsp;
clearly, as all of you Fellow Scholar see right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:12.080
here, this is not the quality of geometry that you&nbsp;
would put into those fancy triple A quality games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:18.840
but at this point I feel that we are just two&nbsp;
more papers away from that kind of detail.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:26.480
Now, there is plenty to love here, and somehow,&nbsp;
it gets even better. We can even write a prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:34.000
and if we would like to refine the results, we can&nbsp;
rewrite parts of the prompt and get a very similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:41.080
result. It works great with this baby bunny, but&nbsp;
I’ll note that if we modify the prompt too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:47.240
we might get an entirely different scene,&nbsp;
so this one requires a light touch.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:52.240
And it gets even better. We can have&nbsp;
a collection of photos of our cat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:57.240
and then, ask the AI to create&nbsp;
a virtual version of this cat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:04.280
but riding on a bike. Imagine meeting&nbsp;
your own cat in a video game! Love it.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:10.000
So, when can we try it? Well, NVIDIA&nbsp;
is planning to include it in Picasso,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.400
their generative AI framework, which is&nbsp;
hopefully going to be widely available&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:22.720
soon. It will be part of the Adobe suite too,&nbsp;
quite honestly, this will be everywhere real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.720
soon. What a time to be alive! If you cannot&nbsp;
wait to give it a go, and you wish to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:35.240
notified when it becomes available, that is a&nbsp;
possibility through the link in the description.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:42.520
And one more thing. I have surprising news.&nbsp;
This technique has already been surpassed. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:48.920
you heard it right. The pace of progress in AI&nbsp;
and computer graphics research is so incredible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:54.680
that there is already something even better&nbsp;
than this out there. I’ll give a hint:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.680 --> 00:04:00.600
it is a Gaussian splatting-based technique.&nbsp;
I can’t wait to tell you all about it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.320
the next episode. Subscribe and hit&nbsp;
the bell icon to not miss out on it.

